Falsifies `byte_sink_contract::verification::end_of_stream_is_no_bytes_message`.

The defect: `eof` is built with the bytes opcode, so the end-of-stream first word equals an empty
bytes message and a sink cannot tell the writer is finished.

Expected to fail: the harness's claim that `eof()` differs from `req(OPERATION_BYTES, n)`; Kani
reports it failing at a count of 0.

diff --git a/crates/byte_sink_contract/src/lib.rs b/crates/byte_sink_contract/src/lib.rs
index 94cea17d5..6b826b91e 100644
--- a/crates/byte_sink_contract/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/byte_sink_contract/src/lib.rs
@@ -112,7 +112,7 @@ pub const fn len(w0: u64) -> usize {
 
 /// The first word of an end-of-stream message.
 pub const fn eof() -> u64 {
-    req(OPERATION_EOF, 0)
+    req(OPERATION_BYTES, 0)
 }
 
